WEBVTT

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.420
Aren't you going to eat, Sherlock?

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:20.830
Huh? No. I ate too much yesterday.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:24.830
You've put on a little weight yourself
recently, right? About 7.5 pounds.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.000
I'm surprised he noticed.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.670
Sherlock, you have a visitor.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.620
I'll come down.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.080
Yes, can I help you?

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:47.000
Good day. Is Mr Holmes in?

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.210
Yes. You must be a client. Please...

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.000
If you'll forgive me, you should take
more care not to overindulge.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.920
You seem to have gained
about seven pounds recently.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.210
Huh? How would you know that?

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:07.120
There are signs that your vest
buttons have been enlarged.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.920
Judging by the hasty tailoring,
it appears to have been recent.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:18.210
Assuming from your waist size and height,
it is clear that you have gained seven pounds.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.670
Who are you, exactly?

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.750
Sh-Sherlock!

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.750
Ow...

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:21.870
This now makes it 673 to nothing, Sherly.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:27.460
How long must I wait before
you make me taste defeat?

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:29.170
Damn you, Brother.

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.210
Huh? This is your brother?

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.170
My older brother, Mycroft.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:39.830
Isn't this great, Sherly?
It's a new paint gun my unit developed.

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:42.290
Who cares?! Get out!

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:48.070
A Scandal in the British Empire Act 1

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:47.920
Pardon me...

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:51.670
...but are you really his older brother?

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.710
My brother and I live very different lives.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:03.580
Just drop it. Did you come over
here just to make wisecracks?

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:06.750
I'm here because I wanted to warn you.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.710
Beware of women.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.420
Huh?

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:21.830
Seeing through the lies of a woman is even
harder than tracing the threads of a crime.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:28.210
Be sure not to forget your brother's
words of advice, Sherly.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:38.960
Are you all right? You look pale.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:42.500
I just can't deal with him.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:45.170
He came in a government carriage.

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.920
Does he work at some government
office or something?

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:52.210
<i>Some</i> office? It's not nearly as simple as that.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:58.540
The man <i>is</i> the government.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:01.080
His position is that important?

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:06.330
Aw, let's stop talking about
my brother. Instead, take this.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:07.790
Read it.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:14.370
No date or sender's name on it?

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:19.540
"Tonight at eight o'clock, a certain man
will call upon you to consult on a matter

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:22.370
of the very deepest moment.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:27.960
Your visitor will be wearing a mask,
but I humbly ask that you not take it amiss."

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.000
What do you think, John?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:36.080
First, this is a man's handwriting.
Further, I believe him to be quite well to do.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:40.830
This peculiarly fine paper could not
be had for less than half a crown.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:46.120
You see? You can do it if you try.
You're right about the "peculiarly" part.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.290
Hold it up to the light.

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:53.370
Are these the initials of the paper mill?

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.500
The "PGt" is German for <i>Papiergesellschaft</i> .

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.960
It means "paper company."

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:03.580
And the "Eg" probably stands for "Egria,"

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:06.750
a city in the German-speaking
region of Bohemia.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:11.960
So the man who sent this letter...

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:17.370
...is a masked German
from the Kingdom of Bohemia.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.540
Come in.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:29.960
Forgive me for calling
you in at this late hour...

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:34.290
...Lieutenant Colonel Moriarty.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:37.210
Not at all. What does the director
of the intelligence service

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:40.830
need with me, from the Indian Army?

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:45.620
I understand that you, with limited manpower,
secretly wiped out the distribution routes

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:49.750
of that new kind of opium
that went around London.

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:53.080
You did an internal investigation on me?

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:59.460
Yes. And I found you to be more
than sufficient as a result.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:07.250
I would very much like your assistance.

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:14.710
Irene Adler. Born in America,
the state of New Jersey.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:19.710
Retired following a career as the prima
donna of the Imperial Opera of Warsaw.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:23.210
Publicly, she is known as a
former actress, but secretly,

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:28.210
she is a courtesan, with the royalty and
nobility of many nations as her clientele.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:33.620
I want you to get back certain classified
papers that this woman stole.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:39.500
Are these classified papers
of the letter or contract variety?

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:48.250
They contain something far more
devastating than you can imagine.

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:52.460
It concerns the Crown,
not merely anything personal.

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:58.080
Whomever retrieves these papers will
unavoidably learn what they contain.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:01.870
If he is making such a grand show
of not revealing what is in them,

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.710
then this must be quite the serious affair.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:09.750
Understood, sir. I will handle this.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:13.830
Colonel Moriarty, your orders are as follows:

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:20.080
Retrieve the stolen papers...
and liquidate Irene Adler.

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:28.620
Classified papers, you say?

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:33.710
Yes. Apparently, they are serious
enough to rock the whole nation.

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:38.830
Have there been any demands
from this Adler woman?

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:43.870
No, up to now, there has not been
a single demand or term issued,

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:47.420
and she has remained in hiding,
without making any contact.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:52.170
She stole something so critical,
but has made no demands.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:56.000
What do you make of it, William?

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:16.670
I do hope that you will forgive me
for wearing this mask.

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:23.330
I am the King of Bohemia,
Wilhelm Gottsreich Sigismond von Ormstein.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:24.620
You're a king?!

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:27.620
It was obvious from the moment you came in.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:34.830
I'm sorry. Circumstances being what they are,
I could not very well send another in my place.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:38.540
That's fine. So let's hear it.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:41.290
This happened five years ago.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:46.420
When I was staying in Warsaw,
I fell in love with a woman.

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:49.000
This woman's name...

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.830
...is Irene Adler.

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:52.920
Yeah, yeah, I know.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:55.040
Sherlock, you know this woman?

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:59.170
I've never met her, but she
is famous in the underworld.

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:03.750
So then, what does this woman have over you?

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:07.330
A photograph, which if it were seen by anyone,

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:11.170
they would naturally assume
that we were to be wed.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.370
I like this woman's pluck!

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:16.210
So she's making you pay
for dumping her, is that it?!

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:20.040
Sh-Sherlock! Don't point!

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:24.870
As it happens, I am to marry
another woman before long.

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:26.460
Huh?

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:28.290
But Adler...

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:32.120
...has threatened that she would
first send her the photograph!

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:35.830
I love it! This woman is riveting!

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:41.920
Three hundred pounds in gold...
and a note for seven hundred more.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:47.920
A th-thousand pounds? That would
pay our rent for over ten years.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:53.370
This is the woman's address. I ask you
to please take back the photograph.

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:01.710
I am glad to have met you.

00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:05.540
Good night, Mr Sherlock Holmes.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.710
Perhaps I made that lie a little too elaborate.

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:44.080
However, it needed to be realistic...

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:50.670
...if I am to lead on the greatest
detective in London.

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:57.960
Come and see me soon, Sherlock Holmes.

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:10.750
Forgive me for calling so late.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:16.370
I am Sherlock Holmes, the consulting detective.

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:20.460
There was some plumbing work
performed here in recent days, yes?

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:23.250
Apparently, during that occasion,

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:25.460
a certain criminal wanted for murder
slipped in with the workers,

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:29.500
and concealed an important piece
of evidence within your home.

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:32.210
I ask you to please assist me with the search.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:36.460
What is this?

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:40.870
A smoke bomb. We're going to
make it look like the house is on fire.

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:42.330
On fire?

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:47.540
See here, John. When an unforeseen
incident such as a fire happens,

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:51.420
people instinctively become concerned
about what is most important to them.

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:56.040
It's all right. I've successfully
used this trick before.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:58.960
It all depends now on how Adler responds.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:01.330
This is an urgent matter.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:04.420
Please, I shan't take very long.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:18.120
I thought it might be someone playing a prank.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:22.710
I can scarcely believe the real
Sherlock Holmes is here.

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:30.250
I am a great fan of yours.
My name is Irene Adler.

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:34.620
She's not at all like the profile
I came up with for her.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:39.120
I didn't take her to be such a light-minded,
cheeky woman as this.

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:50.870
You haven't found anything yet?

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:54.620
Are you sure it was hidden in this house?

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:57.500
Yes, there is no question of that.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:59.330
Now, John!

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:04.250
Please wait just a moment longer.
I assure you, I will locate it.

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:10.420
You assure me you'll find it?
Are you certain you can?

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:19.920
I'll burn everything down
before you find any evidence!

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:25.420
Where's Adler?!

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:27.670
She's gone! Where is she?!

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:36.500
Is this what you are looking for,
Mr Great Detective?

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.210
Why that little...

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:42.540
She knew from the outset that
we were looking for that photo!

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:47.460
Sherlock, did you find the photograph?!

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:51.370
Ah, thank heaven! You found it!

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:52.870
Joh--

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:55.540
The operation was a success...

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.120
...Sherlock!

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:02.170
John! Behind you! There really is a fire!

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:06.500
Hmm? Wah! But why?! It was just
supposed to be a smoke bomb!

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:08.540
I thought you said this worked before!

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:12.920
No--that woman has pulled one over on us!

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:15.750
What a terrible thing to do.

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:20.250
Now the photo you were looking for
may have been lost in the fire.

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:28.330
And either way... you're going to answer
for this, Mr Great Detective.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:38.830
See here, Sherlock! What have
you gone and done this time?!

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.500
Wh-Who are you?

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:45.830
My, you must be the lovely landlady.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:49.460
As of today, we're going to be living together.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:51.120
Aren't we, Sherly?

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:53.000
Wha--?!

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:54.630
Gah! Get off me!

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:55.020
Ooh!

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:57.620
She's going to get the wrong idea!

00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:02.000
M-Miss Hudson, it's quite
a long story, actually...

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.420
Yes.

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:07.460
These two gentlemen are greatly indebted to me.

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:11.920
So I would appreciate your
understanding, Mrs Hudson.

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:14.960
That's "Miss," actually, Mrs...?

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:18.960
<i>Miss</i> ... Adler.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:24.870
E-Excuse me, if I might ask, Miss Hudson...?

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:26.330
<i>Now</i> what?!

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:29.370
Do you have any clothes that she might borrow?

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:32.460
Clothes?! Why?!

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:37.210
I am something of an ash-covered
Cinderella at the moment.

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:42.250
Miss Hudson, I do hope that you are not
one of the cruel stepsisters, are you?

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:59.710
She's made contact with Sherlock Holmes.
Just as you predicted, William.

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:01.170
Yes.

00:17:01.170 --> 00:17:08.120
Holmes likely has not the faintest
idea that Adler's very objective

00:17:08.120 --> 00:17:12.330
is to get close to himself,
the greatest detective in all of London.

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.670
The more she is in the public eye,

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:18.250
the greater the chance is that if
she is abducted, or assassinated,

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:21.120
it will turn into a major incident.

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:25.370
Now the British government cannot try
anything heavy-handed against her.

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:29.620
That is likely what Alder is thinking, at least.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:36.540
Now the question is, how safely can
she reach the negotiation table?

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:44.790
What exactly is she after?

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:51.710
It's going to be near impossible
to retrieve the photo like this.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:56.580
About all I can do is keep my eye on her,
to make sure she doesn't send it.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:02.750
Whoo... Let me have a little smoke break.

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:04.710
If you insist.

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:08.170
But after this, we're going
to go to Piccadilly Circus.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:09.830
Suit yourself.

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:11.370
No!

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:14.290
I am definitely going to audition!

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:17.920
Oh, please. Do try to remember something.

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:22.540
The owner of the theatre is my father,
the viscount. Understand?

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:28.460
Commoners will <i>never</i> be aristocrats.
You will never be a star as long as you live.

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:31.920
Yeah, yeah, remember your place!

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:36.580
Hmph, if this keeps going,
they're bound to come to blows.

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:38.580
What a bother.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:44.580
Everyone is supposed to get
an equal chance to audition.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:52.420
You never had any chance to begin with, Kate.

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:55.790
You're scared, aren't you?

00:18:56.750 --> 00:19:00.920
You're anxious that if I audition,
I'll take the lead away from you.

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:02.580
Be quiet.

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.210
That's why you don't want me to audition!

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:06.830
Be quiet!

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.080
It looks like she can't swim!

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:22.330
The sewage canal is where you commoners belong!

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:27.120
Hey, are you serious?

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:35.790
Adler!

00:19:41.170 --> 00:19:45.420
Aw, we're soaked to the skin.

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:50.460
Th-Thank you very much. But your dress...

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:55.540
Do not worry about it.
Your life is much more important.

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:56.920
But never mind me,

00:19:56.920 --> 00:20:01.120
the world of theatre is not
as easy as you may think.

00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:02.460
Huh?

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:08.040
I have seen many parts go to people due
to their connections or family standing.

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.670
Wait, are you...

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:12.830
...Miss Irene Adler?

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:17.330
L-Listen, I...

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:20.040
...want to be a prima donna, just like you are!

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:25.250
In that case, listen to me, Kate,
and remember this.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:28.620
Prove that you are right
through your own talent.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:30.920
If your abilities are powerful enough,

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:33.370
then connections and
family standing won't matter,

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:35.620
and you will win them over!

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:44.670
R-Right!

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:49.330
You're going to catch cold.

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:55.830
Sherly, you're all but naked, aren't you?

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:58.960
Never mind about me, hurry and put these on!

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:10.210
My initial profile has been shattered.

00:21:10.210 --> 00:21:15.040
She's not the sort of person who would
blackmail the king of Bohemia over an affair.

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.750
When you eliminate all other
possibilities one by one,

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:25.830
whatever remains, no matter how
improbable it may be, must be the truth.

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:32.540
We're here, Irene! Hey, wake up!

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:39.250
Whoops...

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:41.040
Please excuse me...

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:46.620
Miss Adler.

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:51.750
What are you standing around for?
Get on in here!

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:54.460
Yeah...

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:39.090
A Scandal in the British Empire Act 2

00:23:33.870 --> 00:23:39.420
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i> :
"A Scandal in the British Empire Act 2."
